{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-80347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-80347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u=8-{x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=8-{x}^{3}$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & -1 & -\\infty  \\\\ u & 9 & \\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\infty }^{9}(-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{9}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{9}^{a}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[2\\sqrt{u}]}_{9}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{9}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\infty  \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-80347" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8635ff79c20337f4cc104a4f71ae888194ddbc191e4aa2b07b9be6b9dd3781b0"} {"question" "q-80347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-80347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["text" "The integral is divergent"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-80347" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The integral is divergent"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-100642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{2z+1}}\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-100642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{2z+1}}\\,\\text{d}z & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{2z+1}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{3}{2}(2z+1)^{2/3}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[(2z+1)^{2/3}]}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }((2a+1)^{2/3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\infty  \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-100642" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8635ff79c20337f4cc104a4f71ae888194ddbc191e4aa2b07b9be6b9dd3781b0"} {"question" "q-100642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-100642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["text" "The integral is divergent"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-100642" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The integral is divergent"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-152056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}+1)^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-152056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u={x}^{3}+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{3}+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}+1)^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{u}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{u}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{-3/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{a}^{3}}}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-152056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8635ff79c20337f4cc104a4f71ae888194ddbc191e4aa2b07b9be6b9dd3781b0"} {"question" "q-152056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-152056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{9}"] ["text" "The integral diverges"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-152056" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-350527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-350527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u=x+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=x+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{(x+1)^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }3{u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}3{u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{3}{4}{u}^{-4}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-4}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{4}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-350527" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8635ff79c20337f4cc104a4f71ae888194ddbc191e4aa2b07b9be6b9dd3781b0"} {"question" "q-350527" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-350527" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-350543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{12}{(5\\theta -1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-350543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we substitute $u=5\\theta -1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=5\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $\\theta \\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=5\\theta -1$ is as follows:\n\n| $\\theta $ | $-\\infty $ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{12}{(5\\theta -1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{12}{5{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{12}{5{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{12}{5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{u}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-{u}^{-1}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{u}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-1)}-\\frac{1}{a}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot (-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-350543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8635ff79c20337f4cc104a4f71ae888194ddbc191e4aa2b07b9be6b9dd3781b0"} {"question" "q-350543" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"} {"question" "q-350543" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029196/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3178f65f3170acc98997f11a81ef1c0fc8166df918837f7df3181175762b697"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1196 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
